        <body>
            <div xml:id="d594">

                <pb facs="0604" n="595" sameAs="frus:frus1938v05/pg595"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">838.51/3616: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Haiti</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Mayer</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Port-au-Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-06-08T13:00:00-05:00">June 8, 1938—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 2:20 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>57. Reference my mail despatch No. 184, June 3.<anchor n="24" xml:id="d594-f1"/>
                    Pixley tells me that Leger has just informed him that he intends to instruct De
                    la Rue today by telegraph to begin negotiations with the Foreign Bondholders
                    Protective Council with regard to continuing the moratorium on the amortization
                    of the 1922 loan.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mayer</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
